WEBVTT

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:12.161
-What sort of creatures are you?
-VOICE 4: Big ones,
-你们是什么人？
-巨人

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:14.538
with the head
of a tiger and a body of a...
脑袋像老虎，身子像…

00:00:14.622 --> 00:00:16.624
-VOICE 2: Different tiger.
-Yeah.
也像老虎

00:00:16.707 --> 00:00:18.751
VOICE 4: You don't want
to mess with us.
你们最好给我老实点

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:20.211
Or what?
否则呢？

00:00:20.294 --> 00:00:22.546
Or I'll claw you to death!
否则我就抓死你们

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.006
(others murmuring in agreement)
否则我就抓死你们

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.426
And I'll ram my tusks
right through you.
我用利齿把你们刺穿

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.970
And I'll gnash you with my teeth.
我把你们撕个稀巴烂

00:00:30.054 --> 00:00:32.389
And I'll bite you
with my fangs. (growls)
我把你们嚼成碎末

00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:35.184
EDMUND: You mean squash us
with your fat bellies?
再用大肚皮把我们压扁

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.394
-Yes!
-Fat bellies? Huh?
没错

00:00:37.478 --> 00:00:38.521
CASPIAN: Tickle us with your toes?
用脚趾给我们挠痒痒？

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:41.899
-Whoa! (grunts)
-(laughs)
用脚趾给我们挠痒痒？

00:00:41.982 --> 00:00:43.984
What have you done with my sister,
you little pipsqueak?
你们对我妹妹做了什么，该死的小矮人

00:00:45.528 --> 00:00:47.655
-Now, calm down.
-Where is she?
别，别激动

00:00:47.738 --> 00:00:49.490
-You better tell him.
-Tell him, Chief.
-赶紧招了吧
-快点，头儿，告诉他吧

00:00:49.573 --> 00:00:51.283
-Tell him.
-In the mansion.
在房子里

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.535
What mansion?
哪幢房子？

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.997
(rumbling, liquid rippling)

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.380
Oh. That mansion.
那幢房子

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:07.341
You know, I'm really getting tired of you
all leaving me behi--
我简直受够了，你们竟然把我一个人…

00:01:07.425 --> 00:01:10.511
-It's the pig.
-The pig's come back.
-是那头猪
-那头猪来了

00:01:10.594 --> 00:01:12.972
This place just gets weirder
and weirder.
这儿越来越莫明其妙了

00:01:13.055 --> 00:01:15.057
Weird?
Him calling us weird?
-莫明其妙？
-他说我们莫明其妙

00:01:16.058 --> 00:01:17.560
The Oppressor!
The Oppressor!
迫害狂…

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:19.603
-(clamoring, gasping)
-The Oppressor! Oppressor!
迫害狂…

00:01:20.771 --> 00:01:21.939
Lucy.
露西

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.483
Your Majesty.
陛下

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.360
Caspian and Edmund.
凯斯宾和埃德蒙

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.864
This is Coriakin. It's his island.
他是克里亚金，本岛的岛主

00:01:29.947 --> 00:01:33.451
That's what he thinks.
You have wronged us, magician.
那是他自封的

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.870
I have not wronged you.
我没有欺骗你们

00:01:35.953 --> 00:01:38.747
I made you invisible
for your own protection.
隐形是为了保护你们

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.624
-Protection?
-That's oppressive!
保护我们

00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:43.669
-Oppressor!
-I have not oppressed you.
我也没有迫害你们

00:01:43.753 --> 00:01:46.046
But you could've... if you'd wanted to.
如果你想迫害就可以迫害

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.339
Begone.
消失吧

00:01:47.423 --> 00:01:49.884
-It's a spell!
-(anxious shouting)
是咒语

00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:52.178
What was that?
那是什么？

00:01:52.261 --> 00:01:54.764
Lint. But don't tell them.
请不要告诉他们

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.515
(frantic chattering)
请不要告诉他们

00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:00.478
-What were those things?
-Dufflepuds.
他们是什么人？

00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:02.980
Right. Of course. Silly me.
当然，这还用说

00:02:03.063 --> 00:02:04.607
DUFFLEPUD: Get out of here!
当然，这还用说

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.651
What did you mean when you said
你说让他们隐形是为了保护他们
此话何解？

00:02:07.735 --> 00:02:09.987
you made them invisible
for their own good?
你说让他们隐形是为了保护他们
此话何解？

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:14.033
It seemed the easiest way
to protect them from the evil.
只有那样才能使他们免受

00:02:15.493 --> 00:02:16.786
You mean the mist?
你指妖雾

00:02:18.412 --> 00:02:20.539
I mean what lies behind the mist.
我指妖雾的始作俑者

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.185
That's quite beautiful.
真漂亮

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:45.272
(horses neighing)

00:02:45.981 --> 00:02:48.651
-(dogs barking)
-(lion roaring)

00:02:49.693 --> 00:02:52.238
I mean, for a make-believe
map of a make-believe world.
我是说对于一个
虚幻世界的虚幻地图而言

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:54.824
There is the source of your troubles.
那里是你们麻烦的根源

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.910
Dark Island.
黑暗岛

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.080
A place where evil lurks.
海妖就在那里出没

00:03:03.374 --> 00:03:06.001
It can take any form.
它可以任意化形
能带给你最恐怖的恶梦

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.629
It can make your
darkest dreams come true.
它可以任意化形
能带给你最恐怖的恶梦

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.550
It seeks to corrupt all goodness...
它试图将所有美德彻底毁灭

00:03:14.009 --> 00:03:16.345
...to steal the light from this world.
让世界变成最黑暗的所在

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.805
How do we stop it?
怎样才能阻止它？

00:03:18.556 --> 00:03:20.349
You must break its spell.
必须打破它的魔咒

00:03:21.559 --> 00:03:23.644
That sword you carry--
你们携带的宝剑，一共有七把

00:03:23.727 --> 00:03:25.438
there are six others.
你们携带的宝剑，一共有七把

00:03:25.521 --> 00:03:27.148
-Have you seen them?
-Yes.
-你亲眼见过？
-是的

00:03:27.231 --> 00:03:29.859
The six lords--
they passed through here?
六位勋爵，都来过此地，对吗？

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.485
Indeed.
是的

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:32.653
Where were they headed?
他们去哪儿了？

00:03:32.736 --> 00:03:34.113
Where I sent them.
去了该去的地方

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.743
To break the spell...
为了打破魔咒

00:03:41.036 --> 00:03:42.788
you must follow the Blue Star...
你们必须追随蓝星

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.875
...to Ramandu's Island.
前往拉曼杜岛

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:50.004
There the seven swords must be
laid at Aslan's table.
然后将七把宝剑
同时放到阿斯兰的餐桌上

00:03:51.547 --> 00:03:54.049
Only then can their true
magical power be released.
只有那样它们才能释放出原始的魔力

00:03:57.094 --> 00:03:58.471
But beware.
请注意

00:03:58.554 --> 00:04:01.599
You are all about to be tested.
在此期间你们都将接受真正的考验

00:04:01.682 --> 00:04:02.850
Tested?
考验？

00:04:05.561 --> 00:04:10.065
Until you lay down the seventh sword,
evil has the upper hand.
直到将第七把宝剑放到餐桌上
海妖才能彻底被控制

00:04:11.275 --> 00:04:15.613
It will do everything
in its power to tempt you.
千方百计地…

00:04:22.244 --> 00:04:23.537
Be strong.
要坚强

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.750
Don't fall to temptation.
要经得起诱惑

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.128
To defeat the darkness out there...
若想铲除外界的黑暗

00:04:32.546 --> 00:04:34.715
...you must defeat the darkness
inside yourself.
首先要铲除自己心里的黑暗

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:45.976
(whooshing)

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.770
(thunder rumbling)

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:56.487
-(crewmen shouting)
-(thunder crashing)

00:05:04.829 --> 00:05:06.956
EUSTACE: For reasons
beyond my comprehension,
不知到底因为什么

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.625
we've taken the advice
of a senile, old coot
我们竟然接受了那老家伙的建议

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:11.627
who doesn't possess a razor
他连剃须刀都没有
整天穿着睡衣四处游荡

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.963
and dawdles around
in a dressing gown.
他连剃须刀都没有
整天穿着睡衣四处游荡

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:17.800
So we're back in this tub
and lost in a tempest.
于是我们又重新回到船上
在狂风暴雨中挺进，天哪

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:19.135
Brilliant.
于是我们又重新回到船上
在狂风暴雨中挺进，天哪

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.511
-Hold!
-(crewman shouting)
稳住

00:05:20.594 --> 00:05:22.430
(ship creaking)
稳住

00:05:22.513 --> 00:05:25.558
-Three spokes to starboard!
-Aye, aye, sir!
右舵三

00:05:25.641 --> 00:05:27.852
-More pails here!
-Pass it down!
多些桶

00:05:27.935 --> 00:05:31.230
-(crewmen shouting)
-Heave!
拉起来

00:05:31.313 --> 00:05:33.816
EUSTACE: Fourteen days
of being tossed like a pancake
整整14天，我们好像成了上帝的弃儿
完全看不到陆地的影子

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:36.235
and not the slightest sign of land.
整整14天，我们好像成了上帝的弃儿
完全看不到陆地的影子

00:05:36.318 --> 00:05:38.195
(crewmen shouting)

00:05:40.489 --> 00:05:44.535
The only consolation is everyone
is finally as miserable as I am.
所有人都变得和我一样悲惨

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.999
Except for that show-off talking rat.
除了那只一贯爱出风头的老鼠

00:05:50.541 --> 00:05:54.086
He's one of those annoying
glass-is-always-half-full types.
他是那种看到一点亮光
就非说是太阳的家伙

00:05:58.007 --> 00:06:00.676
So, we're stuck here.
眼下我们困在这里

00:06:02.303 --> 00:06:06.223
At half rations, with food and water
for two more weeks, maximum.
给养严重不足
食物和淡水最多还能支撑两周

00:06:08.184 --> 00:06:10.770
This is your last chance
to turn back, Your Majesties.
现在是返航的最后机会了，陛下

00:06:11.812 --> 00:06:14.774
There's no guarantee we'll spot
the Blue Star anytime soon.
我们没有丝毫把握
能够在最近几天看到蓝星

00:06:14.857 --> 00:06:16.233
Not in this storm.
暴风雨太强了

00:06:17.026 --> 00:06:20.279
Needle in a haystack,
trying to find this Ramandu place.
找到拉曼杜岛简直就像大海捞针一样

00:06:20.362 --> 00:06:22.948
We could sail right past it
and off the edge of the world.
我们很可能永远也找不到它的位置

00:06:23.032 --> 00:06:24.909
Or get eaten by a sea serpent.
而且有可能被海妖吃掉

00:06:24.992 --> 00:06:26.869
(thunder rumbling)
而且有可能被海妖吃掉

00:06:27.703 --> 00:06:29.872
I'm just saying,
the men are getting nervous.
我想说大家都感到很紧张

00:06:30.915 --> 00:06:35.586
These are strange seas we're sailing,
the likes of which I've never seen before.
我们行驶在完全陌生的海域

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.882
Then perhaps, Captain, you would like
to be the one to explain to Mr. Rhince
如此说来，船长
也许你应该去告诉莱恩先生

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:41.759
that we're abandoning the search
for his family.
我们必须放弃寻找他的亲人了

00:06:44.929 --> 00:06:46.055
I'll get back to it.
我回去工作

00:06:50.017 --> 00:06:51.102
Just a word of warning.
我只想提个醒而已

00:06:53.187 --> 00:06:55.981
The sea can play nasty tricks
on a crew's mind.
大海会给水手的心理造成恶劣影响

00:06:57.399 --> 00:06:58.943
Very nasty.
非常恶劣

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:05.116
(crewmen shouting commands)

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.206
(lamp squeaking)

